<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chickasaw Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1721–1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chickasaw Wars were fought in the eighteenth century between the Chickasaw, allied with the British, and the French of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> with their Choctaw allies in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> valley. French invasions of the Chickasaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> in northern Mississippi were defeated at Ackia and Ogoula Tchetoka in 1736, and later expeditions also failed. The Chickasaw remained independent until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> in 1763.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chickasaw-wars.jpg" alt="Chickasaw Wars" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MississippiChickasaw1711.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
